## Maintainer verification (2026-10-08)

Merged current main `52217853a2954408d8a88e7ae00b6325badab1f1` because the delivery-plan owner changed. Candidate: `27b3e06315e5b2322c33ce0de259dd1225dbe4a3`.

- Production `persistMatrixDeliveryPlan` → real SQLite blob store → `loadMatrixDeliveryPlan`, isolated in Docker: a valid `durable hello` plan round-trips on both versions. Replacing its separating space byte with `0xff` is accepted on current-main's loader as `durable�hello`; the candidate throws `MatrixDeliveryPlanInvariantError` before returning a plan. This is loader-boundary proof, not a claim of a live Matrix homeserver send.
- `pnpm test extensions/matrix/src/matrix/delivery-plan.test.ts --maxWorkers=1`: 12/12 passed, 34.38 seconds wrapper wall time (Vitest 32.96 seconds, including cold worker compilation). Includes terminal rejection/no-send/cleanup and valid replay coverage.
- Available historical CI seconds at the prior head: `checks-node-changed-extensions-config-6` 134 seconds and `checks-node-changed-extensions-bundle-1` 309 seconds, from run https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/35714698970 . These are job durations, not per-file timings or candidate-head results; per-file CI seconds are unavailable.
- Real `pnpm tsgo` passed (10.76 seconds).
- One real `gpt-5-mini` provider request passed with low reasoning and a 4096-token output budget. This is provider availability proof, not Matrix delivery proof.
- No overlap with Pash/Sarah changes.

The writer, plan version, fields, keys, TTL and serialization are unchanged. No stored-format change or migration is needed. Credit remains with RileyJJY for the repair and regression.

Merge danger: two-way door for code; reverting restores permissive decoding, without changing the stored format. Blast radius is Matrix recovery of malformed durable plan bytes; valid persisted plans retain their behavior.
